        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "I do hear the Members cautioning us that the world is not perfect, and we should not expect a perfect agreement. In the pursuit of perfection, we find an excuse for paralysis. I hear these things, and we will try our best to balance all these cautionary warnings. The road to success is not a smooth one. One overriding topic that came up again is that we all embrace and accept that we must have an agreement. It is critical that we do. We all embrace that and we are on the same page, on the same road, on the same journey. We all believe that it is possible to achieve an agreement, and we all believe that the elements are already on the table, that we have to find a way of preserving our national interests, while at the same time working together for a better world."
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
